l":"https://api.github.com/users/wahan-h/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wahan-h/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T13:07:32Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T13:12:05Z","body":"@akien-mga \n\nit is definitely not fixed... (4.6.1)\n<img width=\"790\" height=\"624\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7a2059d1-37bc-4de3-a2cf-2cf29c2e7225\" />\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4162522049/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6247134294","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111038#issuecomment-6247134294","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111038","id":6247134294,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABdFu0Vg","user":{"login":"diesellaws","id":1047027,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDcwMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1047027?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/diesellaws","html_url":"https://github.com/diesellaws","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diesellaws/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diesellaws/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diesellaws/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diesellaws/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diesellaws/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diesellaws/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diesellaws/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diesellaws/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diesellaws/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-18T07:27:49Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T07:27:49Z","body":"I encountered the same retro Windows title bar issue in **Godot 4.7.2 (Compatibility renderer)** on Windows.\n\nIt happened when my game launched in Windowed mode, then automatically switched to Borderless Fullscreen using saved settings. Switching back to Windowed displayed the old-style title bar.\n\nThis didn't happen with Exclusive Fullscreen, or when switching Windowed → Borderless → Windowed manually.\n\nI traced the issue to calling this during startup, after entering Borderless Fullscreen:\n\n```gdscript\nDisplayServer.window_set_flag(DisplayServer.WINDOW_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON_TOP, false)\n```\n\nEven though `ALWAYS_ON_TOP` was already `false`, this appears to trigger an unnecessary native window-style update.\n\n**This workaround resolved the issue for me:**\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _apply_always_on_top(value: bool) -> void:\n    if DisplayServer.window_get_flag(DisplayServer.WINDOW_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON_TOP) == value:\n        return\n\n    DisplayServer.window_set_flag(DisplayServer.WINDOW_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON_TOP, value)\n```\n\nThis avoids reapplying the flag when its value hasn't changed. It may help others who set `ALWAYS_ON_TOP` during startup.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6247134294/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]